Plugin hosting (Epic 3 — host only; no plugins are bundled or shipped):

  raw-radio-studio hosts third-party plugins at runtime through their public
  plugin APIs. Hosting through these public APIs is not a derivative work of the
  hosted plugins and does not subject the host to their licences — this follows
  the reasoned precedent of the Ardour plugin clarification. The application
  ships the host only and bundles no plugin binaries (STUDIO_SPEC NFR-L-5 / D20).

  * VST3 (default) — the VST3 bindings are bundled with JUCE
    (`JUCE_PLUGINHOST_VST3=1`), compiled from JUCE's pinned tree. The VST3 SDK
    itself is licensed under the **MIT** license (Copyright (c) 2025, Steinberg
    Media Technologies GmbH) — a permissive license compatible with AGPLv3 — and
    is compiled into the combined work under those terms. No separate Steinberg
    SDK is vendored or downloaded. Full license text: `LICENSES/VST3-SDK.txt`.
  * LV2 (opt-in) — enabled only when built with `-DRAW_RADIO_STUDIO_ENABLE_LV2=ON`
    (`JUCE_PLUGINHOST_LV2=1`). The LV2 SDK (lv2, lilv, serd, sord, sratom) is
    bundled inside JUCE's pinned tree and is permissively licensed (permissive
    **ISC**-style — compatible with AGPLv3); no system LV2 libraries are
    required. Full license text: `LICENSES/LV2-SDK.txt`.
  * Audio Unit (macOS only) — `JUCE_PLUGINHOST_AU=1`; uses Apple's system Audio
    Unit framework. Not present, and gracefully absent, on Linux/other builds.
  * VST2 — NOT enabled and NOT shipped (decision D24; `JUCE_PLUGINHOST_VST` is
    never defined). CLAP — not supported (NG4).

  Out-of-process plugin *scanning* (FR-MIX-7) uses Tracktion/JUCE child-process
  machinery already present in the pinned dependencies; no new component is
  added. Hosting itself runs in-process (decision D23).

